   "design": "In s1 plot measurements are recorded on tablets and connected callipers, so typing drops. Growth and yield software computes volumes and growth from the plot data, and the forester checks results. Public land cover layers give a starting map that the forester corrects from field maps. The report template takes the tables, and drafted sections must trace every figure to them. Field measurement, mapping, the value estimate and owner contact stay with the forester.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Plot data were typed from paper and volumes calculated by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Tablet plot forms, growth and yield software and free land cover layers.",
   "still_hard": "Mixed stands where standard volume tables fit poorly.",
   "human_edge": "Reading soil from the plants that grow on it.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less typing and calculating; field judgement stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "forest owner",
